/* ============================================================
   Archivo and Jost, served from the Shopify CDN.

   These used to be two link tags to fonts.googleapis.com, one pair
   copied into sections/watchitude-home.liquid and another into
   sections/watchitude-header.liquid. Three things were wrong with
   that: the request went to a third party on every page load, it was
   duplicated in two files that could drift apart, and because both
   copies lived in section files the tags rendered in the document
   body -- so the font CSS was fetched late and text painted in the
   fallback first. This file is loaded from the document head in
   layout/theme.liquid instead, once, for every page.

   No angle brackets anywhere in this comment on purpose: theme-check
   parses a .css.liquid file for markup as well as Liquid, and a bare
   head or body written as a tag in prose reads to it as an element
   that is opened and never closed.

   One file per family, not one per weight. Both faces are variable
   fonts: Google serves a single woff2 covering the whole 100-900
   weight axis, and the four Archivo weights in the old request were
   four @font-face rules pointing at that same file. Declaring the
   axis once gets every weight the theme uses -- Archivo at 400, 500,
   600 and 700, Jost at 700 -- out of 61KB total, and any weight added
   later comes free.

   Latin subset only, which is the range the old request resolved to
   as well. It covers Latin-1, the general punctuation block the copy
   leans on for em dashes and curly quotes, and the currency and
   arrow marks. A language needing Cyrillic, Greek or Vietnamese
   would need its subset added here.

   font-display: swap, so text paints immediately in the fallback and
   swaps when the face arrives rather than hanging invisible. The
   fallback stacks are on --wt-font-body and --wt-font-display in
   sections/watchitude-home.liquid, chosen to be close in metrics.

   Both families are SIL Open Font License 1.1, per the METADATA.pb
   in google/fonts. The license travels with the font: if these are
   ever shipped anywhere but this theme, the OFL text goes with them.
   ============================================================ */

@font-face {
  font-display: swap;
  font-family: 'Archivo';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 100 900;
  src: url('{{ "wt-archivo-var-latin.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA,
    U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193,
    U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
}

@font-face {
  font-display: swap;
  font-family: 'Jost';
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 100 900;
  src: url('{{ "wt-jost-var-latin.woff2" | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
  unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA,
    U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193,
    U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;
}
